1 Overview
**********

The io package contains functions for reading and writing various type
of data files and some additional file utilities.  The main data file
categories are:

   • .csv and other delimited text files.  The funcions csv2cell and
     cell2csv in the io package can process mixed numeric / text data.
     Octave's dlmread/dlmwrite and csvread /csvwrite can only process
     numeric data.

   • Spreadsheet files.  Out of the box, functions are provided for
     reading / writing data and exploring contents from/to .xlsx
     (MS-Excel), .ods (LibreOffice Calc) and .gnm / .gnumeric (Gnumeric)
     spreadsheet files.  For other file formats and sometimes faster
     I/O, external software can be invoked through 'interfaces'.  Note
     that the spreadsheet I/O functions are meant for transferring data;
     formatting etc.  is ignored.

   • JSON Although Octave provides jsonencode and jsondecode functions,
     the io package contains the (contributed) functions fromJSON and
     toJSON that support e.g., complex numeric data and some other
     constructs.  Support for fromJSON and toJSON is limited.

   • Various other, less used formats, often for dedicated software.
     Most of the related functions were kindly provided by external
     contributors.  Support for these functions is also limited, if only
     because the io package maintainers have no access to the pertinent
     SW.


